# fixture use.force: forces a flag no other fixture package's IUSE
# declares by default, so this has zero effect on any other test --
# exercises the fact that global use.force must win over a package.use
# entry trying to disable it (real regenerate() applies self.useforce as
# the literal last step of its own incremental USE walk, strictly after
# the "pkg"/package.use tier -- see dev-libs/globalprecedencepkg and
# portage-repo's own effective_use_flags doc comment).
globalforceflag
